  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 12, P = 19. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[7, 10, 11, 17, 14, 4, 8, 3, 17, 2, 17, 5], [3, 2, 18, 18, 9, 8, 6, 6, 4, 11, 11, 7], [6, 15, 7, 17, 4, 14, 2, 7, 15, 9, 18, 17]], sigma = [8, 7, 4, 9, 2, 10, 11, 1, 0, 3, 5, 6], B = [7, 16, 5, 5, 5, 2, 11, 16, 7, 5, 2, 11].",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data"
  ],
  "date": "2026",
  "novelty": "known_parameters",
  "notes": "Literature baseline: a reproduction of a code published with arXiv:2609.30069, rebuilt from the authors' data repository (https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data/blob/306b31d/codes/reverse_fold/j3l12/specs/reverse_j3l12_p19_k59.json). Not a new construction. The authors report d = 5 as exact. Their lower-bound search output is not in the repository, so this entry carries an upper bound backed by their weight-5 Pauli logical, stored as the witness."
